# Static checks for the Core (core/src), the C every component runs. Every check on here
# reports nothing today, and CI keeps it that way (ci.yml). The driver has Microsoft's own
# code analysis instead (MSBuild RunCodeAnalysis). Off, with why:
# - easily-swappable-parameters: the Core's API takes (buffer, length) pairs by design;
# - signed-bitwise: it flags the literal shift count in `x >> 8`, which is well defined;
# - implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result: its one report is a compile-time
#   _Static_assert whose product fits.
Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  cert-*,
  misc-redundant-expression,
  readability-misleading-indentation
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
